HQC-5 (Hamming Quasi-Cyclic, category 5) — vendored reference implementation

Source:   https://gitlab.com/pqc-hqc/hqc  (official implementation)
Release:  v5.0.0, commit f46e54222ffb76706678a9ec8a43cd2188a12ab1 (2025-08-22)
License:  public domain, see LICENSE (the bundled FIPS 202 code is the
          public-domain PQClean / TweetFips202 Keccak). Free for any use,
          including commercial use and sale.

Files are byte-for-byte copies, flattened into this one directory, of:
  src/common/*.c, src/common/*.h, src/common/hqc-5/api.h,
  src/ref/*.c, src/ref/*.h, src/ref/hqc-5/parameters.h,
  src/ref/hqc-5/reed_solomon.h, lib/fips202/fips202.{c,h}.
Not copied: hqc-1 / hqc-3 parameters, x86_64/ (AVX2), tests, KAT files,
packaging, build files.

../pq_hqc5.c builds them as one translation unit, renames every external
symbol to zxv_hqc5_* (the reference uses short global names such as
sha3_256, shake256, fft, encode that collide with the kernel's Keccak),
redirects the reference PRNG draws to caller-supplied buffers, and
compiles out its debug printf calls.

libc: memcpy/memset/memcmp (<string.h>); <stdio.h> must exist at compile
time (debug printing only; no stdio symbol is linked).

HQC was selected by NIST in March 2025; its FIPS is not yet final, so a
future standard may differ from v5.0.0.

Checked against the official KAT file kats/ref/hqc-5/PQCkemKAT_7333.rsp
(sha256 43dd50d6f91d9d85085558e66e2ec0168b403ded47c6dad43cd2acfddca2f618),
records 0-9: ../test_pq_matrix.c.
